      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Just ran into this issue again, hadn't used Gravity Falloff in a while because of it.\n\nWhen using Gravity Falloff > 0 and Gravity > 0 (e.g. 1 and 1), assuming you are upright when switching into the avatar, laying down on your back will show your Gravity value have a high impact.\n\nWhile maintaining your layed-down pose, a toggle that turns said Physbone script off keeps them in this gravity-affected orientation - oddly enough as well with 'Reset When Disabled' ticked on.\n\nTurning the Physbone script back on takes the graviy-affected orientation as the new Rest Position. Getting yourself upright e.g. via sitting will now show your Gravity value have a high impact - the complete opposite of the initial effect.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
